INT. FERRY TICKET BOOTH - NIGHT

A cramped glass cubicle on a dock. Rain streaks the windows. One heater glows orange.

AGNES VERHOEVEN (60s, cardigan, reading glasses) counts coins into neat towers. She does not look up when the door opens.

A young man, ILYAS BENALI (20s, soaked jacket, duffel bag), steps in and stands dripping on the mat. He holds out a crumpled ticket.

AGNES
Last boat left an hour ago.

ILYAS
It says ten fifteen.

AGNES
It says a lot of things.

He keeps holding the ticket. She finally takes it. Smooths it flat with her thumb. Studies it too long.

Behind Ilyas, the door opens again. A teenage girl, JUNIPER PARK (16, backpack, earbuds), slips in and stands against the wall, pretending not to listen.

ILYAS
My mother is on that island.

AGNES
Then she'll still be there tomorrow.

He slams the duffel onto the counter. Coins jump. Agnes does not flinch. She re-stacks them one by one.

Juniper pulls out an earbud.

JUNIPER
(quietly)
I have a boat.

Both turn to her. She shrugs, suddenly shy.

JUNIPER (CONT'D)
My dad's. It's small. I can take you.

Agnes lays down her glasses. Studies the girl. Then Ilyas. Then the ticket. She tears it in half and slides the pieces across the counter.

AGNES
Refund. Go.

Ilyas stares. Then, wordlessly, he takes the halves and follows Juniper out into the rain.

Agnes watches them disappear. Picks up her coins. Starts again from one.
